A||||15||SS_304||Difference in looks between '88 Fieros?||||1||
Z||000000||SS_304||08-17-2001||05:00 PM||||Since I've been looking around for a 1988 Fiero to purchase, what's the difference in the body styling of the GT, Formula, SE, etc Fiero models, and those with i4's or V6's?<P>For all I know I want to find a Fiero with the hawk-like aero-nose styling with a spoiler on back, like the one in <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/genesismac/f1ero3.jpg" TARGET=_blank>this pic...</A> there's another styling, one with the black luggage holder (?) in place of the spoiler and without an aeronose... I don't want that styling...<P>For the models with the aeronose and spoilers, do they come with i4's? Or...?<P><BR>help is appreciated in indentifying which model i should look for...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroMontreal||08-17-2001||05:29 PM||||What you want is an 88GT.. those come with the 2.8 V6. They are probably the most expensive fieros around!<P>Good luck<BR>-Alex||||reg||1
Z||000002||SS_304||08-17-2001||05:42 PM||||could I find one for under $4,000, good condition?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ronnie||08-17-2001||06:35 PM||||I did!!  Got mine for $2800. You've just got to shop around.||||reg||6
Z||000004||loafer87gt||08-17-2001||06:51 PM||||Hey SS_304, glad to see a another Ars tech guy here. I was just looking through the autotrader classifieds up here in Canada and there is a couple of really sweet low km 88 GT's for sale. There is a  white GT with 68,000 km asnd loaded for 3,900 US in Alberta, and several 87's for around the 2,500 mark. As far as I know there is three different body styles in 88: The coupe, no-aero nose, notchback, with the 2.5 I-4 engine. The other models are the Formula and the GT. The Formula is a coupe style with a unique front fascia, but without all the power options of the GT and with the v6 engine. The GT is the fastback model and has most of the power options and also comes with the v6 standard. Hope this helps you out somewhat||||reg||1
Z||000005||ray b||08-17-2001||08:20 PM||||88 coupe and 88 formula share a nose<BR>only diff is rubber strip underneath<BR>and paint<BR>J in the year spot on vin # 10th digit<BR>or look at rear lower sept arm [s] to tell if 88 car will have 3 tubes earyer car one stamped arm. 88 are getting rare and will cost more but hunting is fun and they are out there if you look hard and are worth it.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
