Z||000011||Oreif||08-18-2001||02:39 PM||||85 GT 86/87 SE had notchback with the areonose and a wing (wing is a seperate option so some V-6's don't have the wing)The GT's had V-6's and the SE's had I4's as standard and V-6's as optional. (many SE's have the V-6 in them)  86-88 GT's had the fastback body style (Like the pic you show) and all had V-6's. The 85 SE (V-6 was optional) and the 88 Formula had the base coupe style body with a V-6. The 88 Formula had the 15" lace wheels (basically the Formula was a GT with the coupe body). 88 visual differences are the lace wheels are different from front to rear. The rear have a 1" lip where the front's are flush with the face. Also 88 GT's have "Monochrome" paint. Which means the whole car is 1 color.<BR>On 85-87 GT's the aero skirt around the bottom is silver. On 86/87 SE's its black.<BR>The only other aeronose car was the 84 Indy Pace car which are white with silver and all had the I4. As for actual color's of cars,<BR>Gold was only used during 86/87.<BR>Med Metallic red was 87/88<BR>Blue was 87 only.<BR>Yellow was 88 only.<BR>I think the 84 pace car and 88 I4's had the I4 with a dual exhaust. All V-6's had dual exhaust look.<BR>Below is a pic of my 86 SE (V-6)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fcol_01_1.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000012||mrfiero||08-18-2001||02:55 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<B>I think the 84 pace car and 88 I4's had the I4 with a dual exhaust. All V-6's had dual exhaust look.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Close, but not quite......the '84 Pace Car and the '86-'87 SE 4-cyls. have the GT dual exhaust "trumpet" tips.  All other 4-cyl Fieros only have a left side exhaust tip.....nothing fancy, just the plain black steel tips.  <P>The Formula and '85 SE V-6 are the only V-6 Fieros with dual plain black steel tips.....all others have the fancy "trumpet" tips.<P>The Formula is a hard car to describe......it is a plain coupe with the Formula option package that includes all of the engine and suspension goodies of the GT (just not the "luxury" items associated with the GT).  It was a $2000 option on the plain coupe.  The bodies and interiors of the '88 coupe and '88 Formula are 100% identical.<P><BR>Base price on an '88 coupe was $8999, Formula was $10999 and the GT was $13999.  It was possible to pay more for a loaded coupe than a stripped down Formula!  <P><p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 08-18-2001).]||||reg||1
